# Sprite effects
@scenario tutorial_lesson_18
@include /definitions/characters.vns
@label start
[mode dialogue standard]
[set ui.dialogueUi project]
[bg room]
[char pip global on]
[set ui.dialogueFadeMs 160]
[stage clear]
[show pip guide point]
pip: An image effect changes how the sprite is drawn. Compare this pose with the effect on and off.
[if !tutorial_still]
[set character.pip.imageEffect pikupiku.lineboil]
[endif]
pip: Look at the sprite outline.
[set character.pip.imageEffect none]
pip: Find the image-effect ID in this script. Set it to none to restore the original sprite.
> Review question -> check
> Back to topics -> return_hub
@label check
pip: What is the clean baseline for judging a sprite effect?
> A different pose and new lighting. -> retry
> The same pose with its effect off. -> correct
> Back to topics -> return_hub
@label retry
[show pip guide curious]
pip: Keeping the input fixed isolates the change the effect makes. Give it another try.
[jump check]
@label correct
[show pip guide cheer]
pip: Keeping the input fixed isolates the change the effect makes.
> Back to topics -> return_hub
> Replay example -> start
@label return_hub
[if !tutorial_done_18]
[flag tutorial_done_18]
[inc tutorial_count]
[endif]
[stage clear]
[goto TutorialHub:topics_page_3]
